pare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/deployments","created_at":"2016-03-18T04:23:44Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T17:56:23Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-12T17:55:46Z","git_url":"git://github.com/storybookjs/storybook.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:storybookjs/storybook.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook","homepage":"https://storybook.js.org","size":1090866,"stargazers_count":88816,"watchers_count":88816,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":9808,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":2246,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["angular","components","design-systems","documentation","html","javascript","react","react-native","stories","storybook","styleguide","svelte","testing","typescript","ui","vite","vue","web-components","webpack","workshop"],"visibility":"public","forks":9808,"open_issues":2246,"watchers":88816,"default_branch":"next","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/pulls/16912","html_url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/pull/16912","diff_url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/pull/16912.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/pull/16912.patch","merged_at":"2022-06-30T09:05:20Z"},"body":"Issue: #15772\r\n\r\n## What I did\r\n\r\nCurrently, when `transformStoriesRawToStoriesHash` creates a `Group`, the group ends up with the `parameters` of its last child story, because the `parameters` are replaced by each `merge`. This PR changes the merge behavior so that the group will have the parameters of its first child story instead (or, more precisely, the first child story where `parameters` is defined).\r\n\r\nThis fixes the behavior described in #15772, since `selectStory()` [uses the `parameters.viewMode` from the group](https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/blob/e6022f09d9f7c4e39726220f2ef4d56b164b6434/lib/api/src/modules/stories.ts#L288-L294) when given the id of a group, even though it's effectively navigating to the group's first child.\r\n\r\nAlternatively, the issue could be fixed in the `selectStory()` logic (by having it use `s.children[0].parameters.viewMode` when navigating to `s.children[0]`), but I thought it might be preferable to fix the discrepancy at the story hash level in case the `parameters` field of story groups is used elsewhere.\r\n\r\n## How to test\r\n\r\nI've updated the stories API unit tests to cover this scenario.\r\n\r\nIf you want to experience the behavior this was intended to fix, try changing `examples/official-storybook/stories/addon-docs/subcomponents.stories.js` to this:\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n  <summary>Stories with different parameters</summary>\r\n\r\n  ```ts\r\n  import React from 'react';\r\n  import { DocgenButton } from '../../components/DocgenButton';\r\n  import { ButtonGroup } from '../../components/ButtonGroup';\r\n\r\n  export default {\r\n    title: 'Addons/Docs/ButtonGroup',\r\n    component: ButtonGroup,\r\n    subcomponents: { DocgenButton },\r\n  };\r\n\r\n  export const DocsMode = () => (\r\n    <ButtonGroup background=\"#eee\">\r\n      <DocgenButton label=\"This should be shown in docs mode\" />\r\n      <DocgenButton label=\"bar\" />\r\n    </ButtonGroup>\r\n  );\r\n\r\n  DocsMode.parameters = { viewMode: 'docs' };\r\n\r\n  export const StoryMode = () => (\r\n    <ButtonGroup background=\"#eee\">\r\n      <DocgenButton label=\"This should be shown in story mode\" />\r\n      <DocgenButton label=\"bar\" />\r\n    </ButtonGroup>\r\n  );\r\n\r\n  StoryMode.parameters = { viewMode: 'story' };\r\n  ```\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nThen run `yarn storybook` and navigate to `http://localhost:9011/?path=/docs/addons-docs-buttongroup`. On the `next` branch, the first story is shown but the `viewMode` from the second story is used. On this PR branch, the first story is shown and its `viewMode` is used, as expected.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/issues/16912/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/issues/16912/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/issues/comments/986286488","html_url":"https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/issues/15772#issuecomment-986286488","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/storybookjs/storybook/issues/15772","id":986286488,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAzqfmc46yYmY","user":{"login":"TrevorBurnham","id":224895,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDg5NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/224895?v=4","gravatar_